#: bin/sparky-stereo-partners:766
msgctxt "@info:shell the command's help"
msgid ""
"sparky-stereo-partners: the Partners page's choices, for the page, for programs and for tests (ORDER 70).\n"
"\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners status [--json]               the engine, its card, the defaults, the programs, the providers\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners resolve --kind KIND [--program DESKTOP-ID] [--shell]\n"
"                                                          who answers: the interface's address, the model, the card's variables\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners set-default KIND [--interface ID] [--model NAME|--no-model]\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners program DESKTOP-ID KIND follow | own [--interface ID] [--model NAME]\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners card auto|cpu|integrated|discrete|profile|pci-...   (the one key, [Render] Partners, as the Graphics page)\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners engine on|off [--engine ollama|llamacpp]\n"
"                                                          a local engine's user service (ollama.service, sparky-stereo-llama-server.service)\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners account [--json] | signin | signout\n"
"                                                          Ollama's service (ollama.com), through the local engine: signed in or not\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners models [--json]               the models the page offers, each with its size from the registry\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners download NAME [--even-if-metered]   the engine downloads one model (its size said first)\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners provider add ID --name NAME --url URL   (the key is read from standard input, kept in KDE Wallet)\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners provider remove ID | provider list [--json]\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners sync                          programs that read a file of their own get the page's choice: Betterbird's\n"
"                                                          ThunderAI (a managed-storage manifest in ~/.mozilla), when Betterbird is installed\n"
"    sparky-stereo-partners install-plan [--engine E] | install [--engine E] [--even-if-metered]\n"
"                                                          (through pkexec: the engine and this computer's runner)\n"
"\n"
"The choices live in sparky-stereo-partnersrc: the system's in /etc/xdg (shipped), the person's in ~/.config, key by key as\n"
"KConfig cascades them; this command writes only the person's file, through kwriteconfig6. Keys never go into either file.\n"
"Exit status: 0 done, 1 not known (a value nobody set), 2 wrong arguments, 3 failed (said, and kept by the problems engine), 4 the\n"
"card cannot be used (sparky-stereo-gpu-env said why), 5 held: the connection is metered or its state could not be read,\n"
"6 another program already uses the engine's address, 7 not signed in to Ollama's service (the address to sign in is printed).\n"
msgstr ""

